  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Associated Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A type may implement the trait exactly once.",
            "`Counter` has one `Item`, permanently.",
            "Placeholder chosen by the implementor, never by the caller."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Versus Generic Params"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "`type Item;`",
                "lines": [
                  "one impl per type",
                  "no call-site annotation",
                  "`Deref::Target`, `Add::Output`"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "`trait Iterator<T>`",
                "lines": [
                  "many impls per type",
                  "every call site annotates",
                  "`From<u8>`, `From<u16>`"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Associated type when there is one natural output per implementor.",
            "Generic parameter when a type should support many.",
            "`From<T>` is the canonical many case — one target, many sources."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "`Add` Uses Both"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "trait Add<Rhs = Self> {",
            "  type Output;  // associated: the result",
            "  fn add(self, rhs: Rhs) -> Self::Output;",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Generic on the right operand, associated on the result.",
            "`Rhs = Self` default: `impl Add for Point` needs no annotation.",
            "`impl Add<Meters> for Millimeters` overrides the default."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Naming Them"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Written",
            "Where"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Self::Item`",
              "inside the trait"
            ],
            [
              "`T::Item`",
              "generic function"
            ],
            [
              "`<T as Iterator>::Item`",
              "ambiguous case"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "fn sum_all<I>(it: I) -> u32",
            "where I: Iterator<Item = u32> { 0 }",
            "// or: where I: Iterator, I::Item: Display"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Equality constraints go in angle brackets, not after a `:`.",
            "Bounding with a trait constrains without pinning the type.",
            "Traits may bound their own: `trait Graph { type Node: Debug + Clone; }`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Under `dyn`, Spell It Out",
          "text": "`Box<dyn Iterator<Item = u32>>` is required — the vtable cannot leave `Item` open."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Associated Types (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "GATs",
          "items": [
            "Generic associated types, stable since 1.65.",
            "`type Item<'a> where Self: 'a;`",
            "Enables lending iterators that yield borrows of themselves."
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Impl For Every Type",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "impl<T: Display> ToString for T {",
            "  fn to_string(&self) -> String { todo!() }",
            "}  // this impl is why 3.to_string() works"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Implements the trait for every type meeting a bound.",
            "Every `Display` type gets `.to_string()` free, forever.",
            "No per-type work, ever again."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Blanket impl in std",
            "Gives you"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Into<U> for T where U: From<T>`",
              "free `.into()`"
            ],
            [
              "`Borrow<T> for T`",
              "reflexive borrow"
            ],
            [
              "`IntoIterator for I: Iterator`",
              "`for` loop bridge"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Never Implement `Into`",
          "text": "Write the `From` impl and the blanket gives you `Into` automatically, in the right direction."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Extension Traits"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "trait Tap: Sized {",
            "  fn tap(self, f: impl FnOnce(&Self))",
            "    -> Self;",
            "}",
            "impl<T> Tap for T {}  // free for all types"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Define a local trait, blanket-impl it onto foreign types.",
            "How `itertools::Itertools` reaches every iterator.",
            "How `futures::StreamExt` reaches every stream — std untouched.",
            "Legal because the trait is local, even as `T` ranges over foreign types."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Conditional Propagation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "impl<T: Clone> MyTrait for Vec<T> {}",
            "// Vec<T> has MyTrait only when T: Clone"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Real Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Write `impl<T: Display> MyTrait for T` and you close the door.",
            "Nobody — including you — can add `impl MyTrait for MyStruct`.",
            "The struct might implement `Display`, so it could overlap."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "E0119",
          "text": "`conflicting implementations of trait `MyTrait` for type `MyStruct``, with the note `upstream crates may add a new impl`."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Blanket Impls",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No specialization on stable — no general blanket plus a faster override.",
            "`min_specialization` is nightly-only.",
            "`impl<T: Foo> X for T` and `impl<T: Bar> X for T` still conflict.",
            "A type could implement both, so the compiler refuses."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Overlap Workarounds",
          "items": [
            "Add a marker type parameter to distinguish.",
            "Or fall back to the wrapper/newtype trick.",
            "Both trade ergonomics for a distinguishing type."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Blanket Only If Derivable",
          "text": "Blanket-impl a trait only when its behavior follows entirely from the bound. If any implementor would want a custom version, do not blanket it."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blankets show under \"Blanket Implementations\" in rustdoc.",
            "They appear on every matching type's page.",
            "Good way to discover what a type gained for free."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Missing `use`",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A trait's methods are invisible until imported.",
            "`no method named `write_all` found` is almost always this.",
            "Fix: `use std::io::Write;` at the top of the file."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Error",
            "Cause",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "E0308",
              "two types from `-> impl Trait`",
              "`Box<dyn>` or enum"
            ],
            [
              "E0038",
              "`-> Self` or generic method",
              "`where Self: Sized`"
            ],
            [
              "E0117",
              "foreign trait + foreign type",
              "newtype"
            ],
            [
              "E0119",
              "over-broad blanket",
              "narrow the bound"
            ],
            [
              "E0599",
              "bound missing in body",
              "add `T: Clone`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "E0599 lies a little: the type has the method, the generic does not know it.",
            "E0038 is about vtable construction.",
            "E0117 is about which crate owns the impl — different failure, different fix."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reflexive-Impl Trap"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "impl<T> From<T> for MyType {}",
            "// clashes with std's impl<T> From<T> for T",
            "// at T = MyType. Enumerate sources instead."
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Performance Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Box<dyn Trait>` in a hot loop: allocation plus indirection, both avoidable.",
            "A generic or an enum would have been free there.",
            "Unnecessary `.clone()` to dodge a borrow error is a smell.",
            "Real fix is usually `&self` instead of `self`, or a lifetime on the return."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Common Mistakes & Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Under-Using Enums"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "match s {",
            "  Shape::Sq(a) => a * a,   // no vtable",
            "  Shape::Circle(r) => 3.14 * r * r,",
            "}  // exhaustiveness checked, no allocation"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "For a small closed set of types, an enum beats `dyn`.",
            "`enum_dispatch` automates converting a trait object design into one.",
            "Forgetting `?Sized`: `fn print<T: Display + ?Sized>(x: &T)` accepts `str`."
          ]
        },
        {
