        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`dyn` also buys compile-time and binary-size savings.",
            "Associated type when one output per implementor.",
            "Generic parameter when a type should support many.",
            "Blanket impl only when behavior is fully derivable from the bound."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Mental Model",
          "text": "Trait = contract. Bound = requirement on a generic. Monomorphization = one copy per type. Vtable = runtime method table. Coherence = one impl per (trait, type) in the whole program."
        }
