  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of RUST FIELD GUIDE. Rust's trait system is one idea — a contract — wired into four different machines: generic bounds, monomorphization, vtables, and coherence. This handbook walks all of them, from `impl Trait for Type` through the orphan rule, object safety, associated types, and the blanket impls that quietly close your API forever. If you have ever stared at E0038, E0117 or E0119 and guessed at the fix, slide 10 is your lookup table.",
